{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/21326-new-to-changeling-the-lost","id":21326,"title":"New to Changeling: the Lost","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-01T15:42:42-08:00","id":21326,"title":"New to Changeling: the Lost","content":"So, I'm familiar with Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage, mostly the CWoD versions. Changeling the Lost looks pretty snazzy, but I'm not sure what sort of campaigns work for them.<br /> <br /> I mean, Vampire lends itself to building an empire and crushing rivals, Werewolf lends itself to monster hunting and epic quests, and Mage lends itself to weird reality bending games that play around with conceptual themes.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure that sort of games Changeling lends itself to.<br /> <br /> My default campaign structure (from D&amp;D) is usually a five step hero's journey. 1) The bewildered bystanders, in over their heads. The goal is to survive. 2) The seasoned veterans, who have survived and strengthened, seek wealth and fortune. The goal is to prosper. 3) Having earned a reputation for wealth and accomplishment, people look up to the heroes as leaders, and bring all their problems to the hero's feet. The goal is to lead. 4) A great threat looms, that could destroy the entire community/kingdom/empire, and it must be defeated. The goal is to protect. 5) The heroes are long retired, having retreated to the mountaintop, sometimes in solitude and contemplation, sometimes in mentorship to younger heroes. Rather than die quietly, however, the old heroes gather once more to go shake the pillars of heaven. The goal is to change.<br /> <br /> I don't know if that structure would work for Changeling. I mean, part 1 could be &quot;escape the hedge&quot; and part 5 could be &quot;seek vengeance on the Fae that created you&quot;<br /> But I'm not sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1026-trudge","name":"trudge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1026_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T17:31:04-08:00","id":21360,"title":"","content":"Changeling, like the other splats, lends itself to many modes of play but I believe if you wanted to sum it up simply it would be 'coming to terms with yourself.' Whether that involves embracing your fae-ness and rushing to fight the Keepers or slipping back into society and balancing your Mask with your Mien is up to the individual.<br /> <br /> With the arc you've stated:<br /> 1: Changelings have escaped their Keepers, made it back to the real world. There is something keeping them from just slipping back into the place they were taken from, be it a fetch, time, or anything else. As an added storytelling benefit, they have powers and now, new enemies. They find a freehold, it's the only safe place, but how safe is it?<br /> 2: They find a bit of equilibrium. The first hurdles have been overcome, maybe a couple fetches or another servant sent by their Keeper. Whether or not they've re-joined their former lives, they now have a place in the real world, and within the freehold. But they're players, so they have a bit more ambition, a bit more potential than NPCs, so they don't have to settle, they can become kings of the freehold, leaders of their courts, tops of their field.<br /> 3: They're not just extras anymore. Whether they're in positions of power and influence, or they've made a name for themselves in other ways (bringing good things to the freehold? slaying local threats? uncovering hidden dangers?), as you said, in some way or another, they lead.<br /> 4: Just as you say. In my own game it is an army base full of hunters. Maybe it's a rival freehold, an organized bunch of privateers, an army of hedge beasts, a single high wyrd/low clarity changeling, a mage, a vampire, or one of the true fae themselves.<br /> 5: Some changelings stick to being ruler, some decide to leave it behind and make something for themselves in the Hedge, some make a niche for themselves in the real world. They did the hero thing (or perhaps not) and now they are not just names, they're legends. They can be called upon to destroy that Fae they never truly destroyed, whose loyalists prey upon the freehold. Or perhaps that Other they dealt with, to learn the secrets of their enemies, has become a Keeper, or something else. Maybe the Keeper of the motley's leader takes their child, their girlfriend, their husband, so the band gets back together.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's pretty simple. The big difference from other splats is that there is a personalized threat, in the form of the Keeper, and rather than separate yourself from the rest of humanity (except for midnight snacks) you have some incentive to put yourself back into it. Which isn't to say you have to, there are changelings who want to become the monster, who refuse to deal with humanity and never set foot out of their freehold or out of the hedge. But the story arc you described easily fits in to changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T18:29:53-08:00","id":21381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trudge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/21326-new-to-changeling-the-lost#post21326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm familiar with Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage, mostly the CWoD versions. Changeling the Lost looks pretty snazzy, but I'm not sure what sort of campaigns work for them.<br /> <br /> I mean, Vampire lends itself to building an empire and crushing rivals, Werewolf lends itself to monster hunting and epic quests, and Mage lends itself to weird reality bending games that play around with conceptual themes.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure that sort of games Changeling lends itself to.<br /> <br /> My default campaign structure (from D&amp;D) is usually a five step hero's journey. 1) The bewildered bystanders, in over their heads. The goal is to survive. 2) The seasoned veterans, who have survived and strengthened, seek wealth and fortune. The goal is to prosper. 3) Having earned a reputation for wealth and accomplishment, people look up to the heroes as leaders, and bring all their problems to the hero's feet. The goal is to lead. 4) A great threat looms, that could destroy the entire community/kingdom/empire, and it must be defeated. The goal is to protect. 5) The heroes are long retired, having retreated to the mountaintop, sometimes in solitude and contemplation, sometimes in mentorship to younger heroes. Rather than die quietly, however, the old heroes gather once more to go shake the pillars of heaven. The goal is to change.<br /> <br /> I don't know if that structure would work for Changeling. I mean, part 1 could be &quot;escape the hedge&quot; and part 5 could be &quot;seek vengeance on the Fae that created you&quot;<br /> But I'm not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>This structure would work pretty excellently. In part because, what with Talecrafting and the way the Wyrd works, the characters might be deliberately trying to create this narrative and use it as a source of power\u2026 But that\u2019s all stuff from a later supplement (<i>Swirds at Dawn) </i>and presumably you've not got your paws on that yet.<br /> <br /> That structure, to me, would start off with them as hedge-fresh, terrified, confused by what they\u2019ve become and what they can do, struggling to take back their lives and deal with the fetches (or to establish new ones from nothing) and other weirdness and finding a way into insular changeling society.<br /> Then they\u2019d have some stability and would seek to find a niche for themselves in the Freehold, possibly even gravitating to leadership within its Courts. They achieve this and naturally learn that such positions have a lot of responsibility and work that must be done. Then it\u2019s time for a True Fae/goblin incursion they have to deal with lest the Freehokd be destroyed and those unlucky enough to survive be dragged back to Arcadia\u2026<br /> <br /> Then, finally, the old changelings (possibly in emeritus positions at Court, or still holding some leadership or other key role, or living quiet lives as unusually spry old people) have to reunite in response to a new threat \u2013 a True Fae they fought before but knew would return, IT-style, perhaps (maybe they defeated the True Fae before and it agreed to leave for fifty years\u2026 and forty-nine years later they\u2019ve got some work to do). A former friend/ally/PC who raised their Wyrd, haemorrhaged Clairty and became a True Fae that knows where they all live\u2026 The Wyrd itself has plans for them and they decide to go against the Freehold and become bridgeburners that are targeting the Wyrd itself. The possibilities are pretty damn great.<br /> <br /> So here are a few of the things you can go for in Changeling \u2013 epic tales that reference or follow fairytales, narrative tropes and suchlike. Paranoid, spy-style thrillers based on distrust and fear of Pivateers/Loyalists fronting for True Fae. Inwardly focused narratives based on the changeling\u2019s family and fetch. Political manoeuvring in the Freehold \u2013 it can be as corrupt as any vampire\u2019s court, or a relatively harmonious organisation or anywhere inbetween. Character can be ambitious, unconcerned with politics or more interested in patching things up. Exploration of the Hedge, encountering its many dangers and wonders. Entering dreams for fun and profit, Inception style, or as just another battleground against the True Fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T19:04:20-08:00","id":22811,"title":"","content":"Also, check out the supplement Equinox Road. It has ideas for the kind of &quot;endgame&quot; scenarios you mentioned, where powerful PCs might consider going back to Arcadia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/243-billionsix","name":"BillionSix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T06:45:26-08:00","id":23109,"title":"","content":"This is good advice, thank you. <br /> <br /> I'll check out Swords at Dawn for info on tale-crafting, for building the arc I'm looking for. Equinox Road also looks good. Really, there aren't that many books, and they all look pretty useful. The line doesn't seem to suffer from much bloat.<br /> <br /> nofather and Eremite, thank you guys very much for the chronicle outline suggestions. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1026-trudge","name":"trudge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1026_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T07:47:46-08:00","id":23147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trudge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/21326-new-to-changeling-the-lost?p=23109#post23109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll check out Swords at Dawn for info on tale-crafting, for building the arc I'm looking for. Equinox Road also looks good. Really, there aren't that many books, and they all look pretty useful. The line doesn't seem to suffer from much bloat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rites of Spring is great for character creation and alternate/extra rules. Almost a must-buy. The Equinox Road I adore, and it's geared towards high-level play mainly, Winter Masques has more character creation options and alternate Courts, Lords of Summar delves into the Courts in more detail and Autumn Nightmares has lots of sample antagonists and some neat rules for Fetches and True Fae,... But on the latter point, Equinox Road has some too. Those three aren't too high priority for a newcomer, IMO.<br /> <br /> Swords at dawn adds Talecrafting, which is a huge gamechanger, and some new Contracts and lots of random things. Dancers in the Dusk is more of an antagonist book, filled with sample Hobs and finally gives more detail on going into dreams and also adds creatures involved in Fate. Hard to rank their importance unless aspects of them really appeal. There's also Goblin Markets, which is pretty self-explanatory in what it's about, and Victorian Lost, which I doubt you'll be too interested in. <br /> <br /> So.... Get Rites of Spring and Equinox Road. Others are much more optional. Autumn Nightmares should probably come last in importance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T08:04:35-08:00","id":23153,"title":"","content":"Victorian Lost has some appeal, because Steampunk Changeling sounds cool. OTOH, I have plenty of other steampunk books (GURPS published a couple really good steampunk books over a decade ago), so I could probably wing that.<br /> <br /> I'll check out Rites of Spring. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1026-trudge","name":"trudge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1026_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T13:19:26-08:00","id":23286,"title":"","content":"When running stories for changelings, remember that you're running stories for characters who're fugitives, and, in some way, still hunted by the Others. Their relationship to the True Fae is what defines the Lost and separates them from humanity. Whether you're looking for ways to fight your Keeper, trying your best to keep away from her, secretly still working with your Keeper because otherwise he'll eat your family or trying to take his place, in some way, all changelings have to deal with the subject matter of being fugitives and survivors of abuse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T12:33:42-08:00","id":27395,"title":"","content":"Victorian Lost is less Steampunk Changeling than it is down and dirty what it was like in the Victorian Age. There's some interesting things too, like how for a lot of Lower Class Lost, the Durance wasn't much worse, and may even have been better, than their lives before. Because, well, for the lower class factory worker, life SUCKED in the Victorian age.<br /> <br /> then the dual elements of Class-ism. With genuine Aristocracy and Fairest. With Fairest a sort of internal Aristocracy.<br /> <br /> It's a very good book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T02:32:28-08:00","id":27849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dulahan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/21326-new-to-changeling-the-lost?p=27395#post27395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Victorian Lost is less Steampunk Changeling than it is down and dirty what it was like in the Victorian Age. There's some interesting things too, like how for a lot of Lower Class Lost, the Durance wasn't much worse, and may even have been better, than their lives before. Because, well, for the lower class factory worker, life SUCKED in the Victorian age.<br /> <br /> then the dual elements of Class-ism. With genuine Aristocracy and Fairest. With Fairest a sort of internal Aristocracy.<br /> <br /> It's a very good book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still need to get this eventually! But that is something I've wanted to see in the books addressed, a lot of humanity had awful lives as either slaves, peasants, cripples, prisoners, torture victims ect. I believe if given the option many would gamble with Faery, or at least view it as a tribulation that over all have been beneficial to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T02:38:29-08:00","id":27851,"title":"","content":"If you find you have to many Options then look to Entitlements, the books contain many and there are some fan made ones around. Entitlements giver your character structure with themes/styles/philosophies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T11:31:06-08:00","id":28140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/21326-new-to-changeling-the-lost?p=27849#post27849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I still need to get this eventually! But that is something I've wanted to see in the books addressed, a lot of humanity had awful lives as either slaves, peasants, cripples, prisoners, torture victims ect. I believe if given the option many would gamble with Faery, or at least view it as a tribulation that over all have been beneficial to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. I mean, worst case... you're doing something as soulnumbing as you used to be, only now you don't feel the fatigue like you did in the Factory. You might even have your injuries healed...<br /> <br /> Best case you go from that to being some sort of pet Fairest type. And everything is better.<br /> <br /> That's why VL is so awesome, the subset that kind of want to go back is a lot bigger. Loyalist might not be entirely bad. Because, well, it is better back there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T11:41:03-08:00","id":28150,"title":"","content":"Hmm this makes me kinda feel like we should have have gotten a proper supplement on Loyalists. I mean I can see their numbers having multiple philosophies, ranging from the Privateers who would sell their own children to the Gentry for boons or to save their own azz, to those that just love Arcadia yet don't want to Force Changelings to go back, to just those crazy Changelings that don't really realize they aren't Fae and have degenerated in Clarity to such a great extent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T14:04:05-08:00","id":28289,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that would be a good book.<br /> <br /> I know I've personally made 'lings that border on Loyalist, as in, did like their Durance, and might even want to go back if it could continue like it was. But on hearing and seeing the other sorts of Durances are no longer so sure about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T18:14:10-08:00","id":28435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dulahan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/21326-new-to-changeling-the-lost?p=28140#post28140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Best case you go from that to being some sort of pet Fairest type. And everything is better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? The Fairest have a Clarity issue because, on average, their durances were a lot more mentally damaging. They were the pets of amoral gods - their forever abused and physically altered 'lovers', the living statues forbidden or unable to move a muscle (going mad inside), the dancers who would be punished by dancing on hot coals if they showed any sign of stopping. None of the Lost who escaped Arcadia had an easy time, but the changeling the Wizened servants loathed as a pampered princess had the attention of their terrible patron. At least others were mostly ignored.<br /> <br /> I personally never liked that idea, that for some it's better in Faerie, even though I see its just to point out just how vile Victorian society and life was for those at the bottom. My favourite NPC Loyalist is Maya Sharptongue, who subverts this so horribly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":452,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","user":"Eremite","date":". 12-12-2013, 06:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T18:48:02-08:00","id":28445,"title":"","content":"It actually says that Fairest had it better during their Durances. Pleasurable beyond measure. Everyone gets punished, but few of the other seemings had the opportunity to experience such mind-blowing pleasures.<br /> <br /> &quot;For the Fairest, one of the most difficult things about their mangled memories of Arcadia is the illicit pleasure of some of them. While most of the Lost remember either endless fear and torment or at best endless drudgery punctuated only by occasional punishments and at most brief moments of reward, many Fairest experienced a greater mixture of pleasure and pain. They were rewarded with ecstasy beyond mortal comprehension when they pleased their masters or mistresses and punished with ghastly torments when their efforts were considered less than satisfactory. In a few cases, these punishments only consisted of an interruption to a series of otherwise endless and vastly addictive pleasures \u2014 or so the stories go.&quot;<br /> <br /> As for a good Durance, I don't think anyone should have an entirely good one, but not everyone has one full of mud and rape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T19:24:38-08:00","id":28469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/21326-new-to-changeling-the-lost?p=28445#post28445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for a good Durance, I don't think anyone should have an entirely good one, but not everyone has one full of mud and rape.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone was suggesting everyone <i>did.</i><br /> <br /> Arcadia is Heaven, peopled with some of the best artisans and warriors and performers around. Arcadia is Hell, bursting with tormentors out of the nightmares of humanity. Arcadia is Paradise, filled with pleasures mortals can literally only dream of. Arcadia is the bleak and dreary land of the dead, beautiful in the melancholy of its residents' half-remembered music. Arcadia is a fairy tale, which is pulled into the eyes and ears and hearts of man. Arcadia is the mind of millions of dead and live and dreaming and waking gods, which man is pulled into. Arcadia is the seat of the Wyrd, which binds all things together \u2014<i>all</i> things.<br /> <br /> It's rather a lot for a human mind to take in even before accounting for any taking-in being a strictly reciprocal process. Faerie is paradoxical and invasive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T04:44:33-08:00","id":28634,"title":"","content":"The thing is you could say the same for the Supernal, but people aren't keen on forcing the notion that Awakening is a trauma to Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T07:18:18-08:00","id":28708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/21326-new-to-changeling-the-lost?p=28634#post28634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is you could say the same for the Supernal</div> </div> </div> </div>Experiencing the Supernal by necessity happens as a singular domain in the Awakening and is consistent enough that it is unlikely at any given point that the Lustrum is being powered by the suffering of slaves and hovering over the actual metaphysical pit of oblivion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but people aren't keen on forcing the notion that Awakening is a trauma to Mages. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Everything I thought I knew was wrong&quot; is rather different in tone from &quot;I was made to live as a songbird for half a century and was sorely punished whenever I did not talk in strict iambic pentameter.&quot; Changelings who take the Durance poorly tend to be the ones that try to leave for Earth. Mages who take the Awakening poorly tend to be <i>Banishers.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T10:14:54-08:00","id":28798,"title":"","content":"The flip side of that is? By simple chance those same amoral sorts might treat you well for the same reasons they treated others horribly. They had no concept what they were doing. The clarity could as well be things were so good. Living in unfathomable luxury fantasy world with wealth and riches that defy description. Food so good everything in the real world tastes like, well, imagine the worst thing you can imagine eating. Fabrics whose touch was rapture so now even the softest silk feels like the roughest, itchiest hair shirt on your skin. Essentially, those for whom is was so much better that the real world is banal and sucks too. Though knowing what they've lost, and how bad others had it, it's still a real life. Loss of heaven could be as maddening as escape from hell. Though even those ones might suddenly find their Keeper mad at them for something as simple as one stray hair not perfectly coiffed. Wearing the wrong color one morning. Taking their first step with the left foot instead of right. Sneezing at the wrong moment. But I've always thought that the Stockholm Syndrome side of things is an equally good storyline. This is a game about those who were kidnapped aftet all, metaphores for many dark things related to such.<br /> <br /> But yeah, the point about how terrible it was for lower class Victorians is a key theme otherwise. Because, well, their lives sucked at both ends. And losing one hell for another is... while still hell, possibly an improvement. Especially with their bodies forged to be capable of the new hell. (compare to the horrible conditions of the factories of Victorian Age. Or Coal mines. Where the air itself might be killing them, let alone the fatigue of 16 hour days with no break).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}